$\blueD{\text{Line }a}$ has points at $(2,0)$ and $(7,4)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{4-0}{7-2} \\\\\\
&=\blueD{\dfrac{4}{5}}
\end{align}$

$\greenD{\text{Line }b}$ has points at $(-7,9)$ and $(1,-1)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{-1-9}{1-(-7)} \\\\\\
&= {\dfrac{-10}{8}}\\\\\\
&=\greenD{-\dfrac{5}{4}}
\end{align}$
